#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:3
msgid "Comparisons"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:7
msgid "pipx vs pip"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:9
msgid ""
"`pip <https://pip.pypa.io>`_ is a general Python package installer. It can "
"install libraries or CLI applications with entry points."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:11
msgid ""
"pipx is a specialized package installer. It can only install packages with "
"CLI entry points."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:12
msgid ""
"pipx and ``pip`` both install packages from `PyPI <https://pypi.org>`_ (or "
"locally)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:13
msgid ""
"pipx relies on ``pip`` and `venv <https://docs.python.org/3/library/"
"venv.html>`_, or on `uv <https://docs.astral.sh/uv/>`_ under the uv backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:15
msgid ""
"pipx replaces a subset of ``pip``'s functionality: it installs CLI "
"applications but not libraries that you import in your code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:17
msgid "You can install pipx with ``pip``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:19
msgid "Example: install pipx with ``pip``, ``pip install --user pipx``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:23
msgid "pipx vs uv tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:25
msgid ""
"Both `uv tool <https://docs.astral.sh/uv/concepts/tools/>`_ and pipx install "
"a Python tool into its own virtual environment and expose the tool's console "
"scripts on ``PATH``. Both have a one-shot run mode (``uvx`` and ``pipx "
"run``); ``uvx`` is ``uv tool run``. They differ in where state lives, which "
"extra commands they ship, and how they handle managed Python."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/comparisons.rst:30
msgid ""
"pipx keeps the same CLI across pip and uv backends; ``pipx install "
"pipx[uv]`` opts you into uv-speed venv creation without changing any "
"commands. ``uv tool`` ships a smaller per-tool surface, then reuses the rest "
"of ``uv`` for free: managed Python, content-addressed cache, "
"lockfiles, :pep:`723` script handling."
msgstr ""

